Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

WPF / BCB6 Format > Horizontal / Vertical Spacing > Make Equal and Center in
Window:
- 水平等距／垂直等距 (3 or more): the outer two stay, the ones between are
  spread so every gap between neighbours is the same
- 在容器中水平置中／垂直置中 (one or several): the selection as one block,
  centred in its container (Panel / GroupBox / form), relative positions kept
- 同大小 (already on the properties panel) is now a command and a menu item
There is no reference control here, the primary may move too. A locked one,
one without its own px position, too few, or different containers: nothing
moves and the status bar says why (never half done). One edit, one undo.

The right-click submenu is renamed 對齊與間距; the properties panel's
multi-select section gets the four buttons (spacing disabled below 3).
A pending arrow nudge is sent before any align, so the order stays right.

Tests: probe (a real trio per axis on HotPlate and Speed: gaps equal, the
outer two unchanged, one edit; centre one, then a block of two; 2 selected /
a locked one refused), smoke (commands + menu -> align to the probe),
panels_render (buttons, disabled below 3), real VS Code (hcenterIn of
sbtExit + spbSave in Panel2 via the command, ONE undo, no save).

